Cell[TextData[{
 "Pieces that are smaller and have less symmetry will have more placement \
possibilities within an empty cube than larger, symmetrical pieces. Thus, \
they will contribute more rows to the matrix. In a 3x3x3 puzzle, if an \
individual puzzle piece were also 3x3x3 there would only be one placement \
possibility, and thus the piece would only have one row in the matrix. (This \
is the most trivial case possible and corresponds to a puzzle with only one \
piece.) \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  GraphicsBox[
   TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["
