Cell["\<\
The solver can then be called directly in a notebook or deployed to Wolfram \
Cloud. If running the GUI in a notebook however, it is best to use the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]DOWNLOAD-DESKTOP-NOTEBOOK.nb\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
attachment or copy the code into a fresh notebook rather than run it in the \
notebook downloaded from the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Get this Notebook\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] option at the bottom of this post. The notebook \
margins necessary for the community post do not leave much space for the GUI \
in the horizontal direction, so it is more pleasantly viewed in a notebook \
with more standard margins. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.944495512233696*^9, 3.944495556856745*^9}, {
  3.944523132066866*^9, 3.944523200952326*^9}, {3.944523231282028*^9, 
  3.94452329423592*^9}, {3.944523324675684*^9, 3.944523599765177*^9}, {
  3.9445236346868343`*^9, 3.944523753143923*^9}, {3.944523792063137*^9, 
  3.9445238895337048`*^9}, {3.9446081934251976`*^9, 3.944608219942503*^9}},
 CellID->388966740,ExpressionUUID->"d1fb4455-6abf-ae43-a098-c5ab17d782f3"],

